<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 33,074 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 33,074 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 33,074 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 34,399 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     July 21</p>
<p>    Export cargo		16,270	18,961</p>
<p>    Import cargo		16,804	15,438</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and four are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Containers		    300   Dubai Confidence	22/7</p>
<p>Containers		    300   Ayubia		    22/7</p>
<p>Gas oil		26,000	 Stavenger Pride	 23/7</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 CSP-10		    27/7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
